@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Four block definitions whose combined internals expose
'                 12+ parts; standard, flow, and proxy ports; nested flow
'                 properties; delegation from outer ports to inner parts;
'                 connector topology crossing block boundaries.
'   usecase:      Teach nested connector topology, delegation, and item
'                 flows with nested flow properties across many parts.
'   complexity:   complex
'   domain:       sysml internal block definition / multi-block internals
' ============================================================================
title Example Internal BDD - Multi-Block Internals

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' Mapping note
'   - block              -> class <<block>>
'   - interface block    -> class <<interfaceBlock>>
'   - standard port      -> port providing/requiring an interface (open stud)
'   - flow port          -> () stud carrying a typed item flow
'   - proxy port         -> port delegating to an inner part
'   - part               -> nested part usage listed inside the block body
'   - delegation         -> dotted connector from an outer port to an inner
'                           part's port (drawn as ..>)
'   - connector          -> --> edge, label = item-flow type + flow properties
'   - nested flow prop.  -> flow property that is itself a structured value
'                           (e.g. EnergyFlow { power, phase { v, f } })
' This INTERNAL-BDD shows the interior parts of four block definitions and
' the item flows crossing their boundaries. A single-block IBD would show
' only ONE of these interiors.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
note over "PowerPlant", "Grid"
  Outer ports delegate to inner parts via
  dotted edges. Solid edges are connectors
  carrying typed item flows. Flow properties
  may be nested (phase.v, phase.f).
end note

class "IHotFluid" <<interfaceBlock>> {
  +stream : FluidFlow { direction = out }
  +return : FluidFlow { direction = in }
}

class "ICoolant" <<interfaceBlock>> {
  +supply : CoolantFlow { direction = in }
  +drain : CoolantFlow { direction = out }
}

class "PowerPlant" <<block>> {
  +hotOut : IHotFluid        '<<proxy>>
  +coldIn : ICoolant         '<<proxy>>
  +gridTie : PowerLink       '<<standard>>
  part reactor : ReactorCore
  part steamGen : SteamGenerator
  part turb1 : Turbine
  part turb2 : Turbine
  part condenser : Condenser
  part bus : PowerBus
}

class "CoolingTower" <<block>> {
  +supply : CoolantFlow      '<<flow>>
  +drain : CoolantFlow       '<<flow>>
  part basin : Basin
  part spray : SprayDeck
  part fan : FanUnit
}

class "Substation" <<block>> {
  +tie : PowerLink           '<<standard>>
  +feeder : PowerLink        '<<standard>>
  part breaker : Breaker
  part xfmr : Transformer
  part meter : MeterUnit
}

class "Grid" <<block>> {
  +feeder : PowerLink        '<<standard>>
  part line : GridLine
}

' Delegations: outer proxy/flow ports to inner parts (dotted).
"PowerPlant" ..> "PowerPlant" : hotOut -> steamGen.hot
"PowerPlant" ..> "PowerPlant" : coldIn -> condenser.cool
"PowerPlant" ..> "PowerPlant" : gridTie -> bus.tie

' Internal connector topology inside PowerPlant crossing parts.
"PowerPlant" -->[color=#darkred] "PowerPlant" : <reactor.hot> HotSteam { temp, pressure }
"PowerPlant" -->[color=#darkred] "PowerPlant" : <steamGen.steam> SteamFlow { massFlow, enthalpy }
"PowerPlant" -->[color=#darkblue] "PowerPlant" : <condenser.water> WaterFlow { rate }
"PowerPlant" -->[color=orange] "PowerPlant" : <bus.out> EnergyFlow { power, phase{v,f} }

' Cross-block item flows between PowerPlant internals and CoolingTower.
"PowerPlant" -(#darkblue)->[color=#darkblue] "CoolingTower" : CoolantFlow { temp, rate }
"CoolingTower" -.[#darkblue].>[color=#darkblue] "PowerPlant" : CoolantReturn { temp }

' Cross-block standard-port link between PowerPlant.bus and Substation.tie.
"PowerPlant" -->[color=orange] "Substation" : EnergyFlow { power, phase{v,f} }

' Substation internal topology and delegation to the Grid.
"Substation" ..> "Substation" : tie -> breaker.in
"Substation" ..> "Substation" : feeder -> xfmr.out
"Substation" -->[color=orange] "Grid" : PowerLink { voltage, frequency }

note right of "IHotFluid"
  INTERFACE BLOCK typing the hotOut proxy
  port of PowerPlant. Declares flow
  properties with direction out (stream)
  and in (return).
end note

note bottom of "PowerPlant"
  6 parts; outer ports hotOut / coldIn are
  PROXY ports delegating to inner parts;
  gridTie is a STANDARD port delegating to
  the PowerBus part. Internal connectors
  carry typed item flows with NESTED flow
  properties (EnergyFlow.phase.v / .f).
end note

note bottom of "Substation"
  Outer STANDARD ports tie and feeder
  delegate to inner parts breaker and xfmr.
end note

@enduml
